# Line endings.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows and built on Linux (Render for the
# backend image, Vercel for the frontend). Without this, git warns on almost
# every commit that "LF will be replaced by CRLF", and files committed from
# different machines produce diffs that are entirely line-ending noise.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text, store it with LF, and check it out
# with the platform's native ending.
* text=auto

# Binaries git must never try to normalise.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
